Short:        Markdown editor with HTML preview
Author:       André Gewert <agewert@ubergeek.de>
Uploader:     André Gewert <agewert@ubergeek.de>
Type:         text/edit
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.2, dev/gui/html_gadget.lha, AISS (toolbar)
Distribution: Aminet

MDEdit is a Markdown editor for AmigaOS 3.2 with a live HTML preview,
built with ReAction. mdtohtml converts Markdown files to HTML pages from
the Shell. Both use md4c, a fast CommonMark compliant parser written in
C, and understand GitHub flavoured Markdown: tables, strikethrough, task
lists, autolinks and footnotes.

MDEdit
------
 - editor (texteditor.gadget) and preview (html.gadget) side by side,
   the bar between them adjusts the split
 - syntax highlighting of headings, emphasis, code, quotes, lists, links,
   tables and HTML in the editor, line numbers on request
 - the preview follows half a second after you stop typing and keeps
   its scroll position; editor and preview scroll together
 - headings get anchors, so "#anchor" links and tables of contents
   work; links to other .md files open them in the editor
 - pictures with relative paths are loaded from the document's drawer
 - open, save, save as, export to HTML (with your own page template)
 - cut, copy, paste, undo, redo; text selected in the preview can be
   copied as well
 - toolbar with AISS images (TBIMAGES:), text buttons if they are
   missing
 - AppWindow: drop a Markdown icon on the window to open it
 - options as tool types or Shell arguments:
   MDEdit [FILE] <name.md> [TEMPLATE <file>] [CHARSET <name>]
          [DIALECT GitHub|CommonMark] [TTF] [NOAUTOREFRESH] [NOSYNC]
          [NOHIGHLIGHT] [LINENUMBERS]
   TTF uses htmlttf.gadget (anti-aliased TrueType fonts) for the preview.

mdtohtml
--------
   mdtohtml [FROM] <file.md> [TO <file.html>] [TEMPLATE <file>]
            [CHARSET <name>] [TITLE <text>] [DIALECT GitHub|CommonMark]

Without FROM the text is read from standard input, without TO the page
goes to standard output. The title defaults to the first heading. The
charset is only written into the page: UTF-8 if the text is valid UTF-8,
otherwise ISO-8859-1. Raw HTML in the text is passed through.

A template is an HTML file with the placeholders $title$, $encoding$ and
$body$, see Template.html.

Installation
------------
Copy MDEdit (with its icon) and C/mdtohtml wherever you like, e.g. to
SYS:Tools and C:. html.gadget must be installed in SYS:Classes/Gadgets/
or lie next to MDEdit. Example.md has MDEdit as default tool; set the
default tool of your Markdown icons to MDEdit to open them with a
double click.

Contents
--------
 MDEdit               the editor
 C/mdtohtml           the Shell converter
 Example.md           Markdown example
 Template.html        example page template
 Docs/                documentation (English ReadMe.md, German
                      LiesMich.md)
 Icons/               the archive's icons as GlowIcons and NewIcons (and
                      the classic ones); double click UseGlowIcons,
                      UseNewIcons or UseClassic to switch
 Source/              complete source code (C, cross compiled with
                      bebbo's amiga-gcc and NDK 3.2), including md4c

